WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.769
-Our next guest
is a talented musician and actor

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.504
you know from the Showtime
series

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.373
"On Becoming a God
in Central Florida."

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:09.442
She stars in "Monarch," which
airs Tuesday nights on Fox.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.010
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.879
-I hate that everything
has to be a competition.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.347
I love Nikki.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.948
-Well, so do I,
but what can I say?

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.683
People like a little
"Game of Thrones"

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:19.151
with their country music.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:21.487
When your mama
won her first crown,

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:25.725
she sang circles
around both Reba and Dolly.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.360
-I appreciate the support.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.695
I'm going to go out there
and do my best,

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:32.298
but this is not a competition
and there is no rivalry.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.369
-Her naivety is adorable.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.637
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.605
our friend Beth Ditto,
everybody!

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.841 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:48.881 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:55.922 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.823
Beth, it has been too long!

00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:00.326
You haven't been here
since 2019,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.994
and then you were supposed
to come and you got COVID.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.362
How was your recovery?

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.464
-I am -- You know what's weird?
You want to really know?

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:06.833
-Yeah, get into it.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.802
-They told me I have eight
minutes. I was like, "Okay."

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.638
The funny thing
is I have this, like --

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:14.773
'Cause, you know, with COVID,
everybody was depressed, right?

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:16.976
Like, really -- I mean...

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.511
-Yeah, yeah,
I think you've nailed it.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.679
-Yeah.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.813
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.515
I'm very smart.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.384
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:30.022
So, anyway,
but, like, it made me, like --

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.792
I came out of it --
Like, as soon as I got COVID.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.827
And then I got better,
and it was -- that was --

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:37.563
All the depression through
the pandemic and isolation.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:41.467
Look at how I'm sitting.
I'm like -- plbt!

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.403
I've got thighs that touch,

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:49.008
and so putting 'em together
is an effort.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.977
And that's not --
I'm not trying to be funny.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.812
That's just the truth.
-Okay.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.614
That's good. That's good.
Back story.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.516
-Okay. Thank you.

00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:01.520
So, yeah, so it made me --
it made me --

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.922
I came out of it.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.623
Like, after I got over COVID,
a couple days later,

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.093
I had this like --
I went and got my hair done

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.995
with my friend
because I'm cheap.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:12.265
Ordered the hair on Amazon.
Just like this wig.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:15.601
And that's not an Amazon
commercial 'cause -- But --

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.437
-By the way, if it was
an Amazon commercial...

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.604
-$90.

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.206
-...I think they
might have had some notes.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.541
-Yeah.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.810
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.179
Who? Elon?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:31.518
-Yeah. No. Jeff.
Yeah. Elon is Tesla.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:34.854
-The band?
-Yeah, he's Tesla.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.122
♪ Signs, signs,
everywhere the signs ♪

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:40.159
Y'all are young.
Y'all are young.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.463
-Oh, my God.
That is Elon Musk in Tesla.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.930
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:48.367
-Oh, my God!
-Oh, my God!

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.002
So you come out of COVID.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.771
-Yeah, I came out of it,
and I felt like myself again.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.007
-Mm-hmm. That's good.
-Something happened.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.109
Like, there's -- Did you have
that relief when you had it?

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.011
I'm sorry you had it.
-Uh-huh, thank you.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.812
I did.
-That you got it?

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.681
-Yeah.
-Yeah, so I had that.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.882
But then this thing happened

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.216
where I knew I was coming
to see you.

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.585
-Mm-hmm.
-And then that was such a joy.

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.654
And then, like,
doing interviews and stuff.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.889
I just love people so much,
you know?

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:12.692
-It's really nice to be
back with them, isn't it?

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.959
-Yeah, yeah.
-It is really nice.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.761
-I want to tell you something.
-Yeah, go.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.363
-You listen to me.
-I am.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.565
-Ya handsome little devil.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.400
-I watch your show.
You know this.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.203
-Uh-huh.
-I love television. I love it.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.906
And during COVID,

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:30.042
I feel a little touched --
But y'all watch the show.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:33.879
When you say, "We love you,"
to every--

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.581
I'm getting choked up about it.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.249
I was always like,

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:38.751
"There are people
in their apartments right now.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.486
There are people in their house,
they're isolated,

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:41.987
and no one is telling them
they love them."

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.857
You know, it's really important,
and I really mean it.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.959
-That's very sweet of you
to say.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.227
-Yeah. I'm lying.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.062
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.497
My PR people were like,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.667
"This is gonna
hit the nail on the head!"

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.103
That's not true.
I never listen to them.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.037
They're always like,
"Beth, don't say this."

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:00.773
And I'm like, "Okay!"

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.076
-You seem very PR-coached.
-Okay.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.410
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.546
-Everybody's like,
"Where is the real Beth?"

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.881
Hey. Can I ask you a question?
-Yes.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.351
-I know you follow astrology.
You're into it, right?

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:15.321
-Oh. Am I queer
and from Portland?

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:18.991
-Whoo!
-Yes.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:22.829
Can't sling a dead cat
without hitting a witch.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.963
-Okay. So...

00:04:24.963 --> 00:04:26.965
-You want to know a story?
-I would love to.

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:28.768
-Okay. Buckle up, baby.
-You know what?

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.269
I'm gonna just get rid of these.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.804
-Me too.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.606
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.044
-Burn, baby, burn!
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, okay.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.545
-What else was I going to say?

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.680
-Oh, you had actually offered
to babysit my kids, and then

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.717
I heard you babysat your nieces
during the pandemic.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.586
-Doing your "researsh."
"Researsh."

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.754
-I've done my researsh,
as the French say.

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.389
-Bonjour.
-Bonjour.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:52.158
We got a couple of French people
in the audience tonight

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.392
who are looking
for a place to stay.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:55.228
Can they come to your...?

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:58.364
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.833
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.236
It was a real --
Let's just say

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:05.538
it was a real classic
French moment.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.840
Like --

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.542
[French accent]
"I need a place to stay."

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.512
[ Speaking French ]

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:14.847
Where to? Where to?

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.315
"Where to?"
What are you doing?

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.584
-No. [ Speaking French ]
-They're over --

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.586
You can talk to them
in the commercial.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.755
-[ Speaking French ]

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.190
You can live with me tonight.
-Yeah.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.825
[ Speaking French ]

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:30.396
[ Singing in French ]

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.466
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.701
-I just love music. I love it.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.269
-You love music.
-You know what?

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.572
In the -- During the pandemic.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.607
-I just want to shut out
my little nephew Ian,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.009
who's here tonight.
-Really?

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.744
-He's from the town
that my parents grew up in.

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.313
-Okay.
-80 people.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.780
-80 people?
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.249
-And this is in Arkansas?

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.750
-Arkansas.
The oldest town in Arkansas.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.220
-And I've heard you say
that Arkansas in the '90s --

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.956
-It was a cultural hub, honey!

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.791
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.860
Let me ask you something.
-Sure.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.628
-Do you like the smell
of dollar stores?

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.031
-I do. I do.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.133
-I know where you need to go.
-Yeah.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.936
My mom's house --
Hi, mom -- is --

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:12.071
I knew she became
a grandmother when --

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.839
She has so many grandkids.
-Okay.

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.976
-I knew she became a grandmother
when I walked into the house

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.679
and it smelled like
a grandma's house.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:22.114
That's not
the smell of my youth.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:25.318
That only happens when your
children give birth to children.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.353
I swear to God.
-Oh, it does --

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:30.256
You don't -- It is not
that the smell preexists.

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.525
-Oh, no, it didn't smell
like that when I was a kid.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.827
-Yeah. Maybe your nose changed.
Do you think that happened?

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.528
-You know what's funny?
Even before COVID,

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.397
I haven't had a sense of smell
in eight years.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:40.999
-Really? So you kind of were
ahead of the curve with COVID.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:42.668
-Listen.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.903
I was.
-You were.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.104
-I was. You're a trend-setter.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:47.506
-Hey. You know what? Thank you!
-You're welcome!

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:50.175
-This is the respect I deserve!
-And we're running out of time.

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:51.377
-I know. I hate it.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.644
-So I'm gonna ask one question
about your show.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:55.948
-Yeah, I'm on it. I'm on it.
It's on Fox.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.717
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.717 --> 00:06:59.485
[ Applause ]

00:07:01.219 --> 00:07:03.122
-I think there's a...

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:05.357
I don't know what more
you can say about it than that.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:09.628
But you -- So you are a singer,
but you came from indie music,

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.029
you came from punk music,

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:12.731
and now you're playing
a country music singer.

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:14.966
Did you have to teach yourself
how to sing like a country --

00:07:14.966 --> 00:07:17.236
I'm genuinely curious
if that came to you naturally.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.838
-Well, no.
-Okay.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:21.374
-No, I think it could have,

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:22.741
if it was coming
from the kind of --

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:25.544
Like, when I signed up
for the project, I was like --

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:27.546
I just want to say also that
whole clip was not about me.

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:29.382
It was about Kevin Cahoon.
And he is so incredible.

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:30.916
-He's a very good actor.
Very funny.

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:32.250
-Do you know him?

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.852
-No, but I thought
he was really good in that.

00:07:33.852 --> 00:07:35.755
-He's an angel. An angel.

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:38.758
Paulie! Hi.

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:40.059
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:41.627
Um...

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:44.096
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.631
He wrote all the material.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.266
-Oh.
-Um, I'm so sorry.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.767
-You don't --
-I'm like, "Waka-waka!"

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:51.070
-You never have to
apologize to me.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.638
I look forward to this.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:56.676
This is my -- You know,
this is a highlight.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:59.244
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:01.347
I mean, it is --
-That makes me happy.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:03.282
And I will babysit your kids.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.583
-Uh, you will not.

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.786
-That Ramona -- Why?!

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.188
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:11.090
I could -- This is what
I don't understand!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.392
-I feel like if I told you three
things on my way out the door,

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.760
they would be out of your head

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.762
by the time
I was in the elevator.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:19.031
-See, you know
what you're wrong about?

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:21.399
-What?
-Everything.

00:08:21.399 --> 00:08:22.868
For real. I can remember.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:25.237
I have an incredible memory.
I remember everything.

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:26.538
Ask anyone.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:29.241
The thing is, you know, like,

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:32.278
I just really --
When it counts, I'm there.

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.879
-Okay. I believe that.
-I really am.

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:35.414
-You know what?
-I've been chewing gum.

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.049
We got to go.
-Yeah, the worst part.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.084
-I gotta go. [ Grunts ]
-Give me your hands.

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:42.554
You guys, this is Beth Ditto,
everybody.

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:45.291
She is one in a million!

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.192
Mwah!

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:48.861
"Monarch" airs Tuesday nights
on Fox.

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.763
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:53.399
Look at her dress!
Look at her dress!

